Unreal Engine is Windows/macOS only. However, the MCP server itself is just a Python process that connects to the UE editor over a network/IPC protocol — it doesn't require UE to be running to *start*. The server can be deployed on Linux, even if the actual UE interaction requires a running UE instance elsewhere. So this is **deployable on Linux** (the server starts), though functional use requires a UE editor connection.

